"Displays a share or composition as equal-sized cells in a fixed grid with a declared unit value.\n\nUse when: A simple percentage or a few shares should feel countable and tangible. Approximate proportion reading is sufficient at the chosen grid resolution.\n\nAvoid when: Fine precision or many tiny categories would be lost through cell rounding.\n\nVisual grammar: Each equal-area cell encodes an equal fraction or count. Fill identifies the part represented by each cell; grid position follows a declared filling order.\n\nBuild: Choose a grid size and state the value represented by one cell. Allocate cells with an explicit rounding rule and preserve the complete denominator. Fill in a consistent order and label exact percentages outside the grid.\n\nCheck: Check the total cell allocation equals the grid capacity. Verify rounding does not falsely imply exact integer percentages. Confirm all panels use the same cell value if compared.\n\nPitfalls: A coarse grid hides small shares or rounds them to zero. Partial cells need clear rules; prefer a bar when decimal precision is essential.\n\nExample: Show a synthetic 63% completion rate on a 10×10 grid with 63 filled cells and the exact percentage beside it.\n\nAlternatives: Pie chart, Isotype chart, 100% stacked bar chart."
